==English==
{{wikipedia|sacrilege}}

===Etymology===
Compare {{m|en|sacrilege}}, Latin {{m|la|sacrilegus}}. From {{der|en|la|sacer}} + {{m|la|legō||steal something sacred}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/sæk.ɹəˈlɪdʒ.əs/|lang=en}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/sæk.ɹəˈlɪdʒ.əs/|/sæk.ɹəˈliːdʒəs/|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|ɪdʒəs|lang=en}}, {{rhymes|iːdʒəs|lang=en}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Committing [[sacrilege]]; acting or speaking very disrespectfully toward what is held to be [[sacred]].

